# {% project_name %}

A [Soroban](https://developers.stellar.org/docs/build/smart-contracts) smart
contract for the Stellar network, generated by
[Lumenprint](https://github.com/LumenAnvil/lumenprint).

A fungible-token skeleton: balances, transfers, minting, burning and supply
accounting, small enough to read in one sitting.

## Read this before deploying

**This contract is a starting point. It has not been audited, and it is not a
standards-compliant token.**

It does not implement the full
[SEP-41 token interface](https://github.com/stellar/stellar-protocol/blob/master/ecosystem/sep-0041.md)
(`soroban_sdk::token::TokenInterface`). Most visibly it has no allowance or
`transfer_from`, which wallets, DEXes and nearly every integration expect — deployed
as-is you get a token that other software does not know how to use.

Two better paths for real work:

- **Wrapping an existing Stellar asset?** Use the built-in [Stellar Asset
  Contract](https://developers.stellar.org/docs/tokens/stellar-asset-contract)
  instead of writing your own.
- **Need a genuinely custom token?** Implement `TokenInterface` in full, consider
  an audited library such as OpenZeppelin's Stellar contracts, and get the result
  audited.

## What it does show

| Concern | Where |
| ------- | ----- |
| Authorization on the account losing value | `from.require_auth()` in `transfer` and `burn` |
| Admin-only privilege | `mint` |
| Per-holder state in `persistent` storage | `DataKey::Balance(Address)` |
| Time-to-live management | `BALANCE_BUMP` / `BALANCE_THRESHOLD` |
| Typed errors instead of panics | the `Error` enum |
| Events for off-chain consumers | `env.events().publish(...)` |

Balances live in `persistent` storage rather than `instance` storage on purpose:
instance storage is one entry shared by the whole contract, so holding every
balance there would grow the contract's footprint without bound and eventually
price every call out of reach.

Note that `mint` may only create tokens and `burn` may only destroy the caller's
own — the admin cannot burn someone else's holdings. That is a deliberate choice,
and the tests pin it down.

