## Prerequisites

```bash
curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh
rustup target add {% rust_target %}
cargo install --locked stellar-cli@{% stellar_cli_version %}
```

## Test

```bash
cargo test
```

## Build

```bash
{% build_command %}
```

Produces `target/{% rust_target %}/release/{% crate_name %}.wasm`. Use this
rather than `cargo build`: the Stellar CLI selects the correct target and
attaches the contract metadata the network expects.

## Deploy

Constructor arguments are supplied at deploy time:

```bash
stellar keys generate --global alice --network testnet --fund

stellar contract deploy \
  --wasm target/{% rust_target %}/release/{% crate_name %}.wasm \
  --source alice \
  --network testnet \
  -- \
  --admin "$(stellar keys address alice)" \
  --decimals 7 \
  --name "Example Token" \
  --symbol EXTK
```

## Where to take it next

- Add `allowance`, `approve` and `transfer_from` to move toward SEP-41.
- Implement `soroban_sdk::token::TokenInterface` so the compiler checks
  conformance for you.
- Decide whether the admin should be able to freeze accounts or be revoked
  entirely, and write the tests for whichever you choose.
